  <diagram id="seq3" name="Stage 3 Sequence Diagram">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2120" pageHeight="4506" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="s1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=20;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;SC2002 Restaurant Rush: Stage 3 Sequence Diagram  -  Serve a VIP during Happy Hour&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="28" width="1400" x="20" y="18" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffcc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;Use case (Stage 3):&lt;/b&gt; the manager switches on Happy Hour as VIP customer 2 orders, then serves, collects payment and checks the result. Taken from tests/victory.txt (base setting).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Starting conditions:&lt;/b&gt; start of turn 4; customer 1 is at t1 waiting to pay, so table t2 is free; Happy Hour has not been used; Host, Waiter and Chef have not acted.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Outcome:&lt;/b&gt; c2 pays $10.80 (Burger $15.00, VIP 10% off, then Happy Hour 20% off) with satisfaction 100 recorded. Game ends VICTORY (5 paid, $77.10, average 83.2).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;How the manager&#39;s choice changes the outcome:&lt;/b&gt; without Happy Hour, c2 drops to 95 at the end of turn 4 and nothing restores it, so 95 is recorded and the bill is $13.50. Happy Hour trades $2.70 of revenue for +5 satisfaction." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="2080" x="20" y="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
